```
table ip filter {
    chain FORWARD {
        type filter hook forward priority filter; policy accept;
        meta l4proto icmp counter packets 2 bytes 168 drop
    }
}
```

A blanket **DROP rule for all forwarded ICMP (proto 1)** was inserted into router2's netfilter FORWARD hook — almost certainly during the maintenance window. The counter (2 pkts / 168 bytes) was freshly incremented by the ping test just run. Router1 has no such rule.

